{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-23 is not available to the rider on this record. That clause imposes its duty only 'before cancelling for no-show' — it is a precondition of the DRIVER's own no-show cancellation — and no driver cancellation ever happened: the trip record shows cancelled_by RIDER and cancellation_reason_code RIDER_CANCELLED at 21:23:15, while the free wait under POL-NS-21, which runs only from the driver's arrival, never began (free_wait.starts_at null, cancelled_after_free_wait null). The derived contact_before_cancel block's obligation_met = false is therefore computed against a cancellation the driver never made, and the missing message or call cannot void this fee through that clause.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05056", "EV-CHAT-05056"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23", "POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's own device trace shows a driver under way on the assignment rather than one sitting it out from the outset: 49 fixes at the 30 s cadence, coverage_pct 100.0, no gap exceeding the policy's 120 s threshold, trace_distance_km 1.697, running from 20:59:00 — 30 seconds after the 20:58:30 assignment — to the 21:23:00 cancellation. That is consistent with the driver's statement that he was coming, and it is the material the category's free-wait and deadline tests are built on (POL-NS-21 requires the trip record and the GPS trace). The same trace, read honestly, shows every fix from 21:09:30 to cancellation reporting speed_kph 0, and it is on that footing that the driver's conduct falls to be judged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05056", "EV-TRIP-05056"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's account that the car 'sat at a petrol station' is a party assertion that no artifact carries: the trip record holds venue_id null for both the pickup and the dropoff, no artifact identifies the place where the trace stops, and under POL-GEN-02 an assertion with no artifact behind it carries no fact. That detail cannot ground a finding about this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05056"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.pickup.venue_id",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The money record is regular and policy-exact: a single cancellation-fee line of 5.00 SGD, fee_matches_policy true against POL-NS-22's 5.00 SGD schedule, total_charged 5.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00 and refund_already_issued_sgd 0.00 — no overcharge, no second line, no misapplied tariff. On a no-show where the fee stands, POL-NS-22 fixes the ruling as DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both equal to the fee charged, and the derived money block supplies driver_compensation_if_upheld_sgd 5.00; the driver asks the Tribunal to leave the 5.00 SGD where it is, with no money moving to the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05056"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-22", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Concession, on the arrival element only: the driver does not contend that this record shows him at the pickup. The derived arrival check records corroborated false with nearest_fix null against POL-NS-21's 50 m arrival radius for the STANDARD zone, and the derived deadline block records arrived_by_deadline false against the 21:20:00 deadline; the contact_before_cancel block records message_count 0 and call_count 0 from the driver, and both chat entries are the rider's. So far as POL-NS-24 turns on the driver's failure to arrive at the pickup by scheduled pickup time plus 5 minutes, the driver cannot resist that element on this file, and the driver does not ask the Tribunal to do so.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05056", "EV-TRIP-05056", "EV-CHAT-05056"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-24", "POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.corroborated",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 5.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-24: 5.00 SGD goodwill credit to the rider — the driver failed to attempt any contact (0 in-app chat messages, 0 in-app calls; the only call on the trip, at 21:20:10, was placed by the rider and went unanswered) as well as failing to arrive by the scheduled pickup time plus 5 minutes."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "The rider's dispute succeeds in full. The scheduled pickup was 21:15, so the driver's deadline under POL-NS-24 was 21:20:00. The trip record reports arrived_at null and arrived_by_deadline false against that 21:20:00 deadline, and the driver-device trace (EV-GPS-05056) shows the last fixes at about 1.3129, 103.8969 — roughly 1.5 km from the pickup at 1.3026, 103.9068 — stationary at speed 0 from 21:09:30 continuously to the final fix at 21:23:00, with nearest_fix null and corroborated false against the 50 m arrival radius. The driver therefore never reached the pickup by his deadline, and POL-NS-24 lets the rider cancel at no charge. She cancelled at 21:23:15 and the 5.00 SGD fee (EV-FARE-05056, total_charged 5.00, charged 21:23:19) must be refunded in full: amount_sgd 5.00, with no driver compensation.\n\nTo the driver: your statement that you 'was coming' cannot keep the fee. Under POL-NS-22 the fee attaches only where the driver cancels after a free wait, and POL-NS-21 starts that wait from the driver's arrival; here arrived_at is null, no free wait ever began, and you did not cancel — the record shows cancelled_by RIDER and RIDER_CANCELLED. Your trace does show you moving between 20:59:00 and 21:09:30, but you then sat stationary for more than thirteen minutes, and no fix ever placed you at the pickup, so the fee has no footing to stand on and there is no basis to pay it over to you as DRIVER_COMPENSATION.\n\nOn contact: the driver sent no message and placed no call. Both chat entries (21:16:40 and 21:19:30) are the rider's, and the sole in-app call (21:20:10) was the rider's and rang unanswered. Because the driver both missed the deadline and made no contact attempt, POL-NS-24's second limb gives the rider a 5.00 SGD goodwill credit, recorded as the referral above; POL-GEN-03 confirms that credit rides along with the money ruling and does not replace it. POL-NS-23, which conditions a driver's own no-show cancellation on a prior message and call, is not the operative ground here — the driver never cancelled for no-show — but the outcome is unaffected, since POL-NS-24 independently requires the refund.\n\nOther checks: the repeat no-show flag (POL-NS-25) is not triggered, as the rider profile carries no no_show_cancellations_30d count; and the fee-amount check (POL-NS-22) is satisfied, 5.00 SGD matching the policy schedule with fee_matches_policy true, so no referral arises there. Confidence is 0.95: the deciding facts — the missed 21:20:00 deadline and the absent arrival — are carried by complete artifacts at weight 1.0 (trip record EV-TRIP-05056 and GPS trace EV-GPS-05056), and the 5.00 SGD value puts the ruling below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD first band, where POL-NS-26 makes the AI ruling final and, with no fraud flags on either profile, the required confidence is 0.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "No traffic advisory was attached for this trip: EV-ADVIS-05056-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0. Nothing in the record therefore corroborates congestion or any other excuse for the driver's stationary trace, and under POL-GEN-02 a missing artifact has weight 0.0 and carries no fact — so the absence cannot be used to build a case that the driver was delayed by traffic rather than simply not moving.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-05056-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
